WEBVTT

1
00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.565
-[sawing] -[cranking]

2
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.102
[squeaking]

3
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.345
[squeaking]

4
00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.721
[squeaking]

5
00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.758
[sniffing]

6
00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.835
[grunting]

7
00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.173
[grunts]

8
00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.453
[cracking]

9
00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.794
[indistinct chatter]

10
00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:47.567
King Norm, Ruler of the North, Titan of the Tundra,

11
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.504
Potentate of the Pole, the Sultan of Snow!

12
00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.572
[phone clicking]

13
00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.407
That's all I got.

14
00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.676
[yawns] Uh-huh.

15
00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:59.546
Wake up, you royal heinie!

16
00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.481
I need food!

17
00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.849
Have you thought about fishing?

18
00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:06.419
Fishing? Hello! I'm a caribou!

19
00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.354
I forage. Lichens, sedges, shrubs.

20
00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.322
[phone vibrates]

21
00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.324
The good stuff. The green stuff. Do you even care?

22
00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.861
Of course I caribou. I mean I care about you.

23
00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.530
You look skinny, Mickey. You been working out?

24
00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:20.633
[scoffs] Skin-- What-- [groans]

25
00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.970
Whoa, what got into him?

26
00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.705
Not food.

27
00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.008
Try paying a little more attention, Norm.

28
00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.477
The crown never rests.

29
00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.248
-Uh-- [groans] -[phone vibrates]

30
00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.718
[groans] It could be my family!

31
00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:41.354
Your family will have to wait until you're done

32
00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.690
-with your kingly duties. -Oh, when is that?

33
00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.491
After you've heard the last complaint

34
00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.426
from your subjects.

35
00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.766
[indistinct chatter]

36
00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.637
[squeaks, chuckles]

37
00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:01.941
[groans]

38
00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.811
The snow is too soft!

39
00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.947
-Uh-huh. -The salmon are not running!

40
00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.416
-Uh-huh. -[phone vibrates]

41
00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.920
And can I call you Mr. Poopy Pants from now on?

42
00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.923
Uh-huh, definitely.

43
00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.592
[laughing]

44
00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.728
What?

45
00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.297
[rumbling]

46
00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.666
Earthquake!

47
00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.434
[all screaming]

48
00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:37.443
Uh... hi?

49
00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:41.881
King Norm, I come before you to ask your approval

50
00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:45.418
so I can partake in the Jubilee festivities this year.

51
00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.988
[indistinct chatter]

52
00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.793
-And you are... -I'm Tiny.

53
00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.798
No, you're not. You're huge!

54
00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.567
That's my name. [chuckles] It's ironic.

55
00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:04.937
[chuckles nervously] Really?

56
00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:08.041
I'm part of the North too,

57
00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:10.076
and I want to be part of the Jubilee.

58
00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.079
Of course. Uh, it makes sense, but--

59
00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.481
But, well, how can I put this politely?

60
00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.883
It's just that you're a...

61
00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.786
I'm a?

62
00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.921
Well, you're a killer... whale.

63
00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:23.890
Everyone's kinda scared of you.

64
00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.392
Me? [chuckles]

65
00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.960
Who's scared of me? [chuckles]

66
00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.397
[laughing]

67
00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:34.600
-[phone vibrates] -Hmm. It's my family!

68
00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.004
-[phone clicking] -[grunting]

69
00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:43.843
[gasps]

70
00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.081
[rumbling]

71
00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.918
[all screaming]

72
00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.554
[phone vibrates]

73
00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.122
[grunts] Ah.

74
00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.993
[gaps] Where are you going?

75
00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.895
[Norm] Um, family.

76
00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:07.033
What? Wait! Your crown!

77
00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:10.970
[indistinct chatter]

78
00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.773
[grunting]

79
00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.181
-[Tiny] Uh-oh. -[farts]

80
00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.852
[Socrates] Oh, I hate Mondays.

81
00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.457
[phone vibrates]

82
00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:32.692
-[chuckles] -[phone beeps]

83
00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.060
Game on, kids.

84
00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:39.699
Chase? Maria? Quinn? Yoo-hoo.

85
00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.804
Ha! Gotcha!

86
00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:46.506
Whoa!

87
00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.608
[chuckles]

88
00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:50.910
Huh?

89
00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.011
[giggling]

90
00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:54.914
Ah-ha!

91
00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:57.116
[giggles]

92
00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:00.153
I've got you now!

93
00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:05.925
-No fair! -[laughing]

94
00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:09.128
Oh! Oh! Oh! [laughs]

95
00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.798
I wonder who that might be.

96
00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.867
[panting]

97
00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:16.502
[laughs]

98
00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.112
[panting]

99
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.648
Whoa!

100
00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.885
Hey, hey! Whoa! [groans]

101
00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:36.556
[laughs] Catch me if you can!

102
00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:38.891
[groans]

103
00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:41.727
Hmm.

104
00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:45.665
[grunts]

105
00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.701
[cracking]

106
00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.641
[grunts]

107
00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:57.910
[chuckles]

108
00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.714
[Chase] Whoa!

109
00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.282
Come to papa bear!

110
00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.017
That's cheating!

111
00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:07.920
You don't win until you catch every last one of us!

112
00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:09.555
[Quinn laughs]

113
00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:12.158
[panting]

114
00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.566
[laughs]

115
00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:24.670
Gotcha!

116
00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.242
I win. [laughs]

117
00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:30.743
[laughs]

118
00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.245
He fell for it!

119
00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.279
Hmm?

120
00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.681
[screams, groans]

121
00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:36.983
Get him, kids!

122
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.651
[laughing]

123
00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:41.187
[Norm] Oh! Oh, it's on now!

124
00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:43.256
I mean business.

125
00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:45.157
[Socrates] Do you?

126
00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:52.198
Uh, it's not what it looks like.

127
00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.602
No. It's worse!

128
00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:58.804
You're the King of the North, Norm.

129
00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:00.106
The King!

130
00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.775
When you placed that crown on your head,

131
00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.243
you took an oath.

132
00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:06.078
Your subjects need you!

133
00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:09.982
And instead, you cavort and frolic?

134
00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:12.752
[sighs] Let's go!

135
00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:16.756
[sighs]

136
00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:19.759
Not again.

137
00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:23.863
-Come on, Dad. Please? -Just five more minutes.

138
00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:27.400
[groans] Sorry, kids. Duty calls.

139
00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.735
I won't be too long this time.

140
00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:31.237
We've heard that before.

141
00:09:33.239 --> 00:09:35.041
I got a little more work to do,

142
00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:36.976
but I promise, when I get home tonight,

143
00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:39.879
we'll play a game of Snow Blast, huh?

144
00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:45.117
Come on, what do you say? You can't pass up Snow Blast!

145
00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:46.319
Huh?

146
00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:49.221
-You promise? -[Norm] I promise.

147
00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:51.357
When have I ever broken a promise?

148
00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:54.293
Since you've been King, all the time.

149
00:09:54.994 --> 00:09:57.830
Well, not anymore. I decree it.

150
00:09:57.863 --> 00:09:59.832
Tonight we will have the greatest game

151
00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:01.701
of Snow Blast in history!

152
00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.973
-You're on! -[indistinct chatter]

153
00:10:07.173 --> 00:10:08.808
Be careful what you wish for,

154
00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:12.211
for I am Norm, King of the Snow Blast!

155
00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:14.680
[laughs]

156
00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:16.082
Oh, grow up.

157
00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:20.786
[kids laughing]

158
00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:26.993
[cracks]

159
00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:29.195
[squeaking]

160
00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:38.004
[groans]

161
00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:41.474
[Jim] Hello, folks!

162
00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:43.976
This year's Jubilee promises to be

163
00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.012
the biggest and best ever

164
00:10:46.045 --> 00:10:48.214
as the new King of the North, Norm,

165
00:10:48.247 --> 00:10:51.350
takes his place in the pantheon of the greats.

166
00:10:51.384 --> 00:10:52.785
Once again,

167
00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:54.420
you're right on point there, Jim.

168
00:10:55.521 --> 00:10:58.791
Definitely in the panth-y-- Python...

169
00:10:58.824 --> 00:11:00.326
[stammers]

170
00:11:00.359 --> 00:11:02.962
Whatever you just said there, Jim.

171
00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:04.463
That's what it is.

172
00:11:04.497 --> 00:11:05.698
[sighs]

173
00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:08.000
This all seems a bit much to me.

174
00:11:08.034 --> 00:11:12.471
Norm, this is the most important duty you will perform!

175
00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:15.408
The King of the North needs to place his crown

176
00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:17.176
on the apex of the tower

177
00:11:17.209 --> 00:11:19.945
at the precise moment of the Jubilee,

178
00:11:19.979 --> 00:11:22.014
guaranteeing peace and abundance

179
00:11:22.048 --> 00:11:23.349
for the coming winter.

180
00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:25.184
That's just silly superstition.

181
00:11:25.217 --> 00:11:27.086
Silly super-- [groans]

182
00:11:27.286 --> 00:11:31.323
This is tradition, the way of the North.

183
00:11:31.924 --> 00:11:35.761
It dates back thousands of years to the North's first King,

184
00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:39.865
Ragmar the First, Olaf the Pungent,

185
00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:41.734
even Herman the Meek,

186
00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:45.171
all fulfilled their kingly duty.

187
00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:48.407
This is our history.

188
00:11:48.441 --> 00:11:50.109
This is your duty,

189
00:11:50.142 --> 00:11:53.212
and we've got a lot of preparations to get ready

190
00:11:53.245 --> 00:11:56.082
for the Jubilee and not a lot of time.

191
00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:59.251
Oh, heavens to polar bear.

192
00:11:59.285 --> 00:12:02.988
I know, Socrates. I know. There are things to be done.

193
00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:05.157
And, hey, your list doesn't look so...

194
00:12:06.926 --> 00:12:08.060
bad.

195
00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.566
Now, I'll tell ya, Rick, these are the very moments

196
00:12:13.599 --> 00:12:15.201
that define a king.

197
00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:17.903
Does Norm have what it takes to protect the North?

198
00:12:17.937 --> 00:12:21.440
Will he be able to lead his team to victory?

199
00:12:21.474 --> 00:12:24.043
Nope, probably not there, Jim.

200
00:12:24.443 --> 00:12:28.848
Norm needs to realize that there's no "I" in "team."

201
00:12:28.881 --> 00:12:31.984
But there is one in "hippopotamus."

202
00:12:34.854 --> 00:12:38.324
Right you are, Rick. For once, right you are.

203
00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:40.059
That's for sure.

204
00:12:44.597 --> 00:12:46.098
[yawns]

205
00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.368
[thud]

206
00:12:49.401 --> 00:12:52.404
[groans] Huh?

207
00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:57.910
[groans] Snow Blast it.

208
00:13:09.188 --> 00:13:11.290
-[Maria] You promise? -[Norm] I promise.

209
00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.259
When have I ever broken a promise?

210
00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:16.195
[Chase laughs] Oh, tonight's gonna be a blast!

211
00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:17.596
[Quinn] Tonight's gonna rule!

212
00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:20.032
[Maria] Tonight, I'm gonna crush all of you!

213
00:13:20.065 --> 00:13:21.233
[laughing]

214
00:13:27.273 --> 00:13:30.543
[sighs] I'm sorry, honey. I'm gonna make it up.

215
00:13:30.576 --> 00:13:32.511
Of course you will, dear.

216
00:13:34.246 --> 00:13:38.083
[laughs] I remember that. We had so much fun that spring.

217
00:13:38.117 --> 00:13:40.319
It was the best vacation ever.

218
00:13:40.352 --> 00:13:41.620
We should do it again!

219
00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:44.490
I mean, after the festival, obviously.

220
00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:47.393
And then I have to tour the West Floe,

221
00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:49.261
and oh, yeah, I got-- I gotta do something

222
00:13:49.295 --> 00:13:50.930
about that herring farm.

223
00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:55.134
[sighs] We're never going on a family vacation again, are we?

224
00:14:02.408 --> 00:14:03.542
[sighs]

225
00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:19.925
[sighs]

226
00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:45.684
[Tiny] ♪ I'm a little teapot ♪

227
00:14:45.718 --> 00:14:48.220
♪ Short and stout

228
00:14:48.254 --> 00:14:50.956
♪ Here is my handle

229
00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.291
♪ Here is my...

230
00:14:53.092 --> 00:14:54.960
[yawns]

231
00:14:57.029 --> 00:14:59.632
[rumbling]

232
00:15:34.366 --> 00:15:36.468
[Norm snoring]

233
00:15:54.586 --> 00:15:56.722
Jubilee... No.

234
00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:05.197
Daddy loves you.

235
00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:09.101
You love Daddy? Yeah?

236
00:16:22.147 --> 00:16:24.283
I'm the King of the Snow Blast!

237
00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:32.658
[Norm snoring]

238
00:16:39.698 --> 00:16:41.200
[seagulls crying]

239
00:16:47.539 --> 00:16:51.243
[snoring]

240
00:16:57.483 --> 00:16:58.584
[yawns]

241
00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:04.323
Good morning, everyone!

242
00:17:16.402 --> 00:17:17.403
Huh?

243
00:17:21.373 --> 00:17:24.877
Uh... Look, about last night, I--

244
00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.880
There you are! Come on! You're needed!

245
00:17:27.913 --> 00:17:29.815
But I haven't even had breakfast.

246
00:17:29.848 --> 00:17:32.084
Later. Let's go.

247
00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.162
[burps]

248
00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:46.899
[Norm] What's the emergency?

249
00:17:46.932 --> 00:17:48.567
There's no time to waste!

250
00:17:48.801 --> 00:17:50.869
Preparations are behind schedule.

251
00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.738
Where's your crown?

252
00:17:53.238 --> 00:17:55.474
Fish on a stick! One second.

253
00:17:59.778 --> 00:18:03.248
[grunting]

254
00:18:07.586 --> 00:18:09.354
[panting]

255
00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.124
What?

256
00:18:12.691 --> 00:18:14.359
[laughs nervously]

257
00:18:16.595 --> 00:18:19.131
[gasps] You lost the crown?

258
00:18:19.465 --> 00:18:21.333
No, I didn't lose it.

259
00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:24.169
I'm just questioning the whole concept of object permanence.

260
00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:25.604
It was there, now it's gone.

261
00:18:26.472 --> 00:18:27.606
Science. Go figure.

262
00:18:27.973 --> 00:18:30.242
This is a disaster, Norm!

263
00:18:30.275 --> 00:18:31.577
[Elizabeth] Everything okay, honey?

264
00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:35.781
Uh, yeah. Everything's fine, dear.

265
00:18:35.814 --> 00:18:38.350
Perfect. Never better. Livin' the dream.

266
00:18:39.952 --> 00:18:44.189
I told you, Norm. The crown isn't just a symbol!

267
00:18:44.223 --> 00:18:46.492
I know. It's a responsibility.

268
00:18:46.525 --> 00:18:48.460
Apparently, you don't know!

269
00:18:48.494 --> 00:18:50.496
Without the crown, the Jubilee festival

270
00:18:50.529 --> 00:18:52.197
can't be completed.

271
00:18:52.231 --> 00:18:55.267
We're gonna be cursed by an endless winter.

272
00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:58.570
What? That story, it's just a superstition.

273
00:18:58.604 --> 00:19:00.472
It's decreed!

274
00:19:00.506 --> 00:19:02.941
If the King of the North doesn't crown the ice tower

275
00:19:03.408 --> 00:19:05.244
during the Jubilee festival,

276
00:19:05.544 --> 00:19:09.615
an endless winter will fall upon the North.

277
00:19:09.815 --> 00:19:11.650
[bicycle bell dinging]

278
00:19:12.251 --> 00:19:15.287
It's our history, Norm.

279
00:19:15.787 --> 00:19:18.390
That's science.

280
00:19:18.423 --> 00:19:20.359
Oh, well, in that case...

281
00:19:27.566 --> 00:19:28.767
[chuckles]

282
00:19:36.308 --> 00:19:37.342
[squeaks]

283
00:19:43.849 --> 00:19:44.983
Huh?

284
00:19:45.784 --> 00:19:46.919
What is going on?

285
00:19:47.786 --> 00:19:50.489
I lost a contact lens.

286
00:19:51.623 --> 00:19:53.458
You don't wear contact lenses.

287
00:19:53.492 --> 00:19:55.327
Oh. You're right.

288
00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:57.963
What a relief! Mystery solved!

289
00:19:57.996 --> 00:20:01.466
Well, look at the time. I gotta go do king stuff.

290
00:20:04.536 --> 00:20:05.737
[chuckles nervously]

291
00:20:10.475 --> 00:20:14.379
[stammers] Yes. What-- What he said.

292
00:20:17.783 --> 00:20:18.784
[ice crumbles]

293
00:20:19.918 --> 00:20:20.986
Hmm.

294
00:20:23.455 --> 00:20:24.990
Hey, what's this?

295
00:20:25.791 --> 00:20:27.292
Those tracks...

296
00:20:40.872 --> 00:20:43.041
Don't look at me like that.

297
00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:46.545
You can't keep running away from your duties, Norm.

298
00:20:52.384 --> 00:20:54.553
Enough! You're wasting time!

299
00:20:57.022 --> 00:20:59.424
Hey, Tiny! What's up, my whale?

300
00:20:59.458 --> 00:21:02.527
-Can I ask you a question? -I don't know, can you?

301
00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:06.498
May I? I may. I mean, it's really important.

302
00:21:06.531 --> 00:21:08.600
These ski tracks, you didn't, perhaps,

303
00:21:08.634 --> 00:21:09.935
see who made them?

304
00:21:10.502 --> 00:21:13.071
Even if I did, why should I tell you, bear?

305
00:21:13.105 --> 00:21:17.409
What? No, I'm not just a bear. I'm Norm, King of the North.

306
00:21:17.676 --> 00:21:19.611
Norm, where's your crown?

307
00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:21.346
[chuckles] Huh? See?

308
00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.814
I'm having it cleaned.

309
00:21:22.848 --> 00:21:24.683
Look, Tiny, you don't remember seeing

310
00:21:24.716 --> 00:21:27.019
anything suspicious about last night, do you?

311
00:21:27.452 --> 00:21:28.453
[Tiny] Hmm.

312
00:21:28.787 --> 00:21:32.124
Do I remember?

313
00:21:32.157 --> 00:21:34.926
Yeah. Suspicious? Weird? Bizarre?

314
00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:37.696
Oh, I do remember something!

315
00:21:37.896 --> 00:21:39.431
Great! What?

316
00:21:39.464 --> 00:21:41.066
I remember

317
00:21:41.099 --> 00:21:44.836
you not inviting me and my pod to the Jubilee festival!

318
00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.873
Something about us being "killer whales."

319
00:21:51.543 --> 00:21:53.612
I meant that as a compliment.

320
00:21:53.645 --> 00:21:56.581
You know, you're a "killer", whale.

321
00:21:56.615 --> 00:21:59.117
Right. Killer-comma-whale.

322
00:21:59.151 --> 00:22:01.987
Ooh, darn those misplaced modifiers.

323
00:22:02.721 --> 00:22:04.890
-Ask me nicely. -Please.

324
00:22:05.557 --> 00:22:06.792
-Nicer. -Pretty please?

325
00:22:07.025 --> 00:22:08.927
-Nicer. -Pretty please?

326
00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:10.796
With sugar and lemmings on top?

327
00:22:10.996 --> 00:22:12.864
Yeesh. That's kinda gross.

328
00:22:12.898 --> 00:22:16.501
Please tell me, did you see anything?

329
00:22:16.535 --> 00:22:19.738
Well, I do remember a strange ship.

330
00:22:19.771 --> 00:22:20.706
What kind of ship?

331
00:22:21.707 --> 00:22:23.742
It's all so hazy. It might've been a dream.

332
00:22:25.877 --> 00:22:28.380
Oh, let me check my Sonar Chat.

333
00:22:30.749 --> 00:22:32.984
-Sonar Chat? -It's an app.

334
00:22:33.018 --> 00:22:35.620
Whales invented it, and they never fail

335
00:22:35.654 --> 00:22:36.922
to brag about it.

336
00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.726
[whale song]

337
00:22:41.626 --> 00:22:43.862
[beeping]

338
00:22:46.765 --> 00:22:48.433
[pulsing]

339
00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:50.802
[indistinct chatter]

340
00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:52.904
[pulsing]

341
00:22:56.808 --> 00:22:57.809
[beeping]

342
00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:00.545
[grunting]

343
00:23:01.913 --> 00:23:03.815
[pulsing]

344
00:23:03.849 --> 00:23:05.450
[indistinct chatter]

345
00:23:07.519 --> 00:23:09.521
[pulsing]

346
00:23:10.188 --> 00:23:11.656
[grunting]

347
00:23:13.692 --> 00:23:14.659
[beeping]

348
00:23:18.864 --> 00:23:21.600
-[pulsing] -[indistinct chatter]

349
00:23:21.833 --> 00:23:23.468
[pulsing]

350
00:23:25.203 --> 00:23:26.204
[beeping]

351
00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:33.712
[pulsing]

352
00:23:34.112 --> 00:23:36.081
[indistinct chatter]

353
00:23:40.051 --> 00:23:42.888
[barking]

354
00:23:47.793 --> 00:23:49.995
[barking echoes]

355
00:23:50.028 --> 00:23:51.596
[laughs]

356
00:23:54.766 --> 00:23:55.967
I was right!

357
00:23:56.168 --> 00:24:00.172
There was a ship entirely made out of ice.

358
00:24:00.205 --> 00:24:03.208
The strangest ship you'll ever see.

359
00:24:03.241 --> 00:24:04.142
Where?

360
00:24:04.576 --> 00:24:06.812
It's headed towards China,

361
00:24:07.546 --> 00:24:09.581
and it has this symbol on it.

362
00:24:09.614 --> 00:24:12.851
I believe it belongs to the city of Harbin.

363
00:24:13.952 --> 00:24:15.854
-In China? -China.

364
00:24:15.887 --> 00:24:18.190
-China? -Am I saying it wrong?

365
00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:20.525
China.

366
00:24:20.959 --> 00:24:24.129
I've been to China. It's a long way from here.

367
00:24:24.162 --> 00:24:25.964
Well, you better get going then.

368
00:24:32.304 --> 00:24:34.172
Nobody must know you're gone.

369
00:24:34.673 --> 00:24:37.209
What am I gonna tell Elizabeth and the kids?

370
00:24:37.242 --> 00:24:40.045
-Nothing. -I can't lie to my family.

371
00:24:40.078 --> 00:24:42.214
Well, it's not lying if you don't say anything.

372
00:24:42.247 --> 00:24:43.882
I guess so.

373
00:24:43.915 --> 00:24:47.219
But still, Harbin? And I can't tell my family.

374
00:24:48.153 --> 00:24:49.621
We're going to Harbin?

375
00:24:49.654 --> 00:24:51.189
-Where's Harbin? -[phone clicking]

376
00:24:56.795 --> 00:24:59.764
Wow! Dad's taking us on a vacation!

377
00:24:59.798 --> 00:25:01.633
He's trying to make it up to us.

378
00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:03.802
In Harbin, China!

379
00:25:03.835 --> 00:25:06.605
I'd feel really bad if they ever found out.

380
00:25:06.638 --> 00:25:08.173
They won't find out,

381
00:25:08.206 --> 00:25:11.343
and the bigger question is, how are you going to get there?

382
00:25:11.376 --> 00:25:14.012
[Lemmings squeaking]

383
00:25:18.016 --> 00:25:18.984
Really?

384
00:25:19.217 --> 00:25:20.719
[squeaking]

385
00:25:25.190 --> 00:25:27.659
I've gotta go see a moose about an ice floe.

386
00:25:27.692 --> 00:25:31.596
And how about, uh, my sister just had cubs!

387
00:25:31.630 --> 00:25:33.698
Oh, she knows I don't have a sister.

388
00:25:33.732 --> 00:25:35.867
You sly bear, you.

389
00:25:35.901 --> 00:25:37.836
Sly? Me? What?

390
00:25:37.869 --> 00:25:39.905
I know what you're up to.

391
00:25:39.938 --> 00:25:42.274
-You do? -Yeah, we heard everything!

392
00:25:42.307 --> 00:25:43.842
Everything? Uh...

393
00:25:44.109 --> 00:25:46.745
-I don't know what to say. -Me, neither.

394
00:25:46.778 --> 00:25:48.346
Did you really think you could plan

395
00:25:48.380 --> 00:25:50.348
a surprise vacation to Harbin, China

396
00:25:50.382 --> 00:25:52.083
without telling us?

397
00:25:52.117 --> 00:25:53.618
Vaca-- What?

398
00:25:53.652 --> 00:25:54.986
[kids] You rock, Dad!

399
00:25:55.020 --> 00:25:58.156
Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad!

400
00:25:58.189 --> 00:26:01.226
-Dad! Dad! Dad! -Surprise!

401
00:26:01.259 --> 00:26:03.695
Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad!

402
00:26:04.329 --> 00:26:07.299
[squeaking]

403
00:26:15.941 --> 00:26:17.042
[Socrates] Okay.

404
00:26:17.075 --> 00:26:18.977
It's no luxury liner,

405
00:26:19.010 --> 00:26:21.046
but it looks like it'll hold Norm...

406
00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:23.248
and his family?

407
00:26:25.150 --> 00:26:27.385
No use hiding it anymore, Socrates.

408
00:26:27.419 --> 00:26:30.221
They found out about the surprise vacation

409
00:26:30.255 --> 00:26:32.257
that I planned on purpose.

410
00:26:32.457 --> 00:26:35.160
-What? -Ta-da!

411
00:26:35.994 --> 00:26:37.128
[camera clicks]

412
00:26:37.329 --> 00:26:38.630
[chuckles]

413
00:26:39.130 --> 00:26:41.733
Oh. [laughs]

414
00:26:42.167 --> 00:26:44.369
[laughs] Yeah.

415
00:26:44.402 --> 00:26:46.404
This is funny because it's not.

416
00:26:46.438 --> 00:26:47.806
Yeah, just go with it.

417
00:26:47.839 --> 00:26:49.040
What's the worst that can happen?

418
00:26:49.074 --> 00:26:50.041
[camera clicks]

419
00:26:59.351 --> 00:27:00.719
[squeaking]

420
00:27:03.888 --> 00:27:04.789
[gasps]

421
00:27:07.392 --> 00:27:11.830
[squeaking]

422
00:27:18.903 --> 00:27:19.971
We're doomed.

423
00:27:23.508 --> 00:27:27.445
Well, here's a wrinkle in the old Jubilee game plan.

424
00:27:27.479 --> 00:27:30.315
If King Norm doesn't place his crown on top of the tower

425
00:27:30.348 --> 00:27:32.384
by the official beginning of winter,

426
00:27:32.417 --> 00:27:33.818
chaos will ensue.

427
00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:37.288
We're talkin' about the end of the North as we know it.

428
00:27:37.322 --> 00:27:41.059
You're talking about polar bears eating polar bears?

429
00:27:41.092 --> 00:27:43.028
Lemmings eating lemmings?

430
00:27:43.061 --> 00:27:45.397
A muskrat eating, like, a muskox?

431
00:27:45.897 --> 00:27:46.898
Yes, Rick.

432
00:27:47.999 --> 00:27:50.335
We're talking about an endless winter of disaster.

433
00:27:51.936 --> 00:27:53.138
[squeaking]

434
00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:58.309
[foghorn blows]

435
00:28:06.051 --> 00:28:08.720
[humming]

436
00:28:09.854 --> 00:28:12.524
[yawns, sniffing]

437
00:28:12.557 --> 00:28:14.025
-[farts] -Gross!

438
00:28:14.059 --> 00:28:16.795
Get your nasty foot away from my face.

439
00:28:16.828 --> 00:28:19.364
Well, if Quinn would move his elbow.

440
00:28:19.397 --> 00:28:22.400
[grunting]

441
00:28:22.434 --> 00:28:25.437
-Stop kicking! Quinn? -It wasn't me.

442
00:28:25.470 --> 00:28:28.473
-Chase? -[gasps] He's lying!

443
00:28:28.506 --> 00:28:30.175
[grunting]

444
00:28:30.208 --> 00:28:31.976
What is going on out here?

445
00:28:32.010 --> 00:28:33.445
Family photo op!

446
00:28:33.478 --> 00:28:36.414
I borrowed this from Vera for our new family portrait.

447
00:28:36.448 --> 00:28:37.749
Come on, kids. Everyone in.

448
00:28:39.984 --> 00:28:41.820
-Perfect. -[beeps]

449
00:28:41.853 --> 00:28:43.955
Everyone say, "Harbin!"

450
00:28:44.322 --> 00:28:45.490
-[beeps] -Huh?

451
00:28:46.491 --> 00:28:47.892
[beeping]

452
00:28:47.926 --> 00:28:49.227
[all] Harbin!

453
00:28:49.427 --> 00:28:50.929
[beeping]

454
00:28:50.962 --> 00:28:51.963
-[camera clicks] -Norm?

455
00:28:52.330 --> 00:28:54.866
Sorry, it's just, uh...

456
00:28:55.133 --> 00:28:56.234
I'll be back.

457
00:28:59.838 --> 00:29:01.406
-Honey? -[Norm] Be right down.

458
00:29:08.146 --> 00:29:12.517
Huh? You dirty, dastardly, despicable...

459
00:29:13.184 --> 00:29:16.054
-Dear! -What are you doing, Norm?

460
00:29:16.087 --> 00:29:18.223
Oh, you know, looking for the perfect sunset.

461
00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:20.158
For the picture.

462
00:29:20.191 --> 00:29:21.993
I just want the light to be perfect.

463
00:29:23.928 --> 00:29:26.164
Aw, you do care!

464
00:29:26.197 --> 00:29:29.601
Of course I do, honey. I'm a bear that cares.

465
00:29:29.634 --> 00:29:32.237
Bearing is caring, right?

466
00:29:33.204 --> 00:29:35.306
Okay. Places, everyone.

467
00:29:55.093 --> 00:29:57.162
[beeps]

468
00:30:07.238 --> 00:30:10.375
Hey, Elizabeth, mind if I set the shot?

469
00:30:10.408 --> 00:30:11.643
Of course not.

470
00:30:11.676 --> 00:30:14.179
[grunting]

471
00:30:16.247 --> 00:30:17.182
[camera whirs]

472
00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:20.952
-[screams] -What's wrong, dear?

473
00:30:21.386 --> 00:30:24.556
Nothing. It's just the composition is all wrong.

474
00:30:24.589 --> 00:30:27.292
The background, the lighting. This just won't do.

475
00:30:31.429 --> 00:30:34.332
Crew, this is your captain, port to bow.

476
00:30:34.365 --> 00:30:36.167
I mean, starboard to aft.

477
00:30:36.201 --> 00:30:40.171
I mean, turn this tub around! Lemmings, abort! Abort!

478
00:30:40.205 --> 00:30:41.606
Norm, the background is fine.

479
00:30:45.143 --> 00:30:46.277
A little to the left.

480
00:30:51.316 --> 00:30:53.351
Too far. No, a little to the right.

481
00:30:54.485 --> 00:30:55.653
[Norm] Uh...

482
00:30:57.355 --> 00:30:58.890
[beeps]

483
00:31:02.594 --> 00:31:04.262
Everyone say--

484
00:31:04.295 --> 00:31:06.197
-Jump! -[beeping]

485
00:31:10.301 --> 00:31:12.003
[beeping]

486
00:31:12.036 --> 00:31:13.238
[camera clicks]

487
00:31:13.271 --> 00:31:14.505
Cheese.

488
00:31:18.443 --> 00:31:19.544
[sighs]

489
00:31:19.577 --> 00:31:21.980
[ice crackling]

490
00:31:29.153 --> 00:31:31.256
[screams]

491
00:31:35.326 --> 00:31:36.628
[Quinn] Dad, where's the water?

492
00:31:36.661 --> 00:31:38.329
[Chase] How are we gonna get to land?

493
00:31:38.363 --> 00:31:40.598
I don't know. Guys, guys, it's just an inconvenience.

494
00:31:40.632 --> 00:31:42.133
I've got this.

495
00:31:43.101 --> 00:31:44.602
-[beeps] -Fong?

496
00:31:44.636 --> 00:31:46.471
Hey, buddy!

497
00:31:46.504 --> 00:31:48.606
How's the vacation going so far?

498
00:31:48.640 --> 00:31:51.442
It's very, uh, ice.

499
00:31:51.476 --> 00:31:54.178
Uh, don't you mean very "nice"?

500
00:31:54.212 --> 00:31:56.381
No, I mean very "ice."

501
00:32:00.451 --> 00:32:03.254
Oh, dear! I'm on my way.

502
00:32:03.288 --> 00:32:05.990
[helicopter whirring]

503
00:32:36.654 --> 00:32:39.691
Wakey wakey, eggs and bakey!

504
00:32:41.092 --> 00:32:43.628
[yawning]

505
00:32:46.064 --> 00:32:47.765
[yawns]

506
00:32:49.701 --> 00:32:52.570
Welcome to Harbin!

507
00:32:58.276 --> 00:33:00.445
This looks amazing!

508
00:33:00.478 --> 00:33:04.582
See? You give your Dad lemons and he makes vacation-ade!

509
00:33:06.718 --> 00:33:09.787
[kids] Wow! Whoa!

510
00:33:09.821 --> 00:33:11.656
[Quinn] That's mega cool!

511
00:33:26.637 --> 00:33:29.707
Wait! Hold up. Let's stay together.

512
00:33:29.741 --> 00:33:31.275
-I got Maria. -I'm on Chase.

513
00:33:31.642 --> 00:33:34.345
You guys vacation hardcore.

514
00:33:35.780 --> 00:33:37.081
Norm?

515
00:33:37.749 --> 00:33:39.183
[laughs]

516
00:33:39.217 --> 00:33:40.518
Excuse me. Pardon me.

517
00:33:55.199 --> 00:33:56.667
[howls]

518
00:33:57.835 --> 00:33:58.803
[barks]

519
00:34:03.641 --> 00:34:04.675
[barks]

520
00:34:06.277 --> 00:34:07.612
[grunts]

521
00:34:07.645 --> 00:34:08.713
[slurps]

522
00:34:09.147 --> 00:34:10.114
[burps]

523
00:34:18.156 --> 00:34:19.590
[gasps]

524
00:34:23.428 --> 00:34:24.429
Ah!

525
00:34:24.729 --> 00:34:26.431
[squeaking]

526
00:34:36.841 --> 00:34:38.576
[laughing]

527
00:34:41.379 --> 00:34:42.413
Chase?

528
00:34:43.314 --> 00:34:44.415
Chase?

529
00:34:46.384 --> 00:34:47.752
[laughs]

530
00:34:53.357 --> 00:34:54.325
Ha!

531
00:34:55.359 --> 00:34:56.394
[giggles]

532
00:34:59.230 --> 00:35:00.364
[panting]

533
00:35:01.866 --> 00:35:03.134
[pants]

534
00:35:05.470 --> 00:35:07.305
[laughs]

535
00:35:09.240 --> 00:35:12.276
[music playing]

536
00:35:20.485 --> 00:35:22.753
Uh, Maria, what are you doing?

537
00:35:22.787 --> 00:35:24.322
The Watusi!

538
00:35:24.355 --> 00:35:25.590
What are you doing?

539
00:35:26.724 --> 00:35:31.462
Oh, oh! I don't know. These beats are taking me over.

540
00:35:31.963 --> 00:35:35.500
Watch yourself. [grunting]

541
00:35:36.267 --> 00:35:40.271
-[record scratching] -[dance music playing]

542
00:35:42.907 --> 00:35:44.509
Back it up, back it up.

543
00:35:44.842 --> 00:35:46.544
[grunting]

544
00:35:46.744 --> 00:35:49.280
-[seal groans] -Oh, sorry about your foot.

545
00:35:51.649 --> 00:35:52.917
♪ Let's do it! ♪

546
00:35:54.619 --> 00:35:55.786
♪ Let's do it now!

547
00:35:58.756 --> 00:36:00.458
♪ Let's do it!

548
00:36:00.491 --> 00:36:02.426
Watch out! Watch out! Watch out! Watch out!

549
00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:03.828
Watch out! There it is!

550
00:36:06.531 --> 00:36:08.666
-♪ Let's shake it -♪ Hey!

551
00:36:08.699 --> 00:36:10.935
♪ Shake it, shake it

552
00:36:10.968 --> 00:36:13.638
♪ Work it, work it Gotta work it now ♪

553
00:36:13.905 --> 00:36:16.374
♪ Shake it, shake it, shake it ♪

554
00:36:16.407 --> 00:36:17.808
♪ You know ya wanna

555
00:36:17.842 --> 00:36:19.477
♪ Shake it, shake it

556
00:36:20.578 --> 00:36:21.746
♪ Let's do it

557
00:36:22.446 --> 00:36:25.616
♪ Oh, let's work it now

558
00:36:25.816 --> 00:36:27.251
Watch me go! Watch me go!

559
00:36:27.451 --> 00:36:28.753
♪ Let's do it

560
00:36:30.755 --> 00:36:32.823
♪ Let's do it now

561
00:36:33.057 --> 00:36:35.326
[laughs] Face it, Maria.

562
00:36:35.359 --> 00:36:37.495
Your old man's still got the moves.

563
00:36:37.528 --> 00:36:39.463
[applause]

564
00:36:39.697 --> 00:36:40.865
Maria?

565
00:36:41.299 --> 00:36:44.936
[cheers and applause]

566
00:36:50.908 --> 00:36:52.276
Huh?

567
00:36:53.778 --> 00:36:54.946
Hmm.

568
00:36:54.979 --> 00:36:56.380
[gasps]

569
00:37:00.718 --> 00:37:03.287
[grunting]

570
00:37:04.922 --> 00:37:08.259
[Maria laughs] Are you okay?

571
00:37:08.526 --> 00:37:11.929
[grunting]

572
00:37:15.433 --> 00:37:16.901
I'm fine.

573
00:37:16.934 --> 00:37:17.902
Huh?

574
00:37:18.102 --> 00:37:19.470
Those tracks.

575
00:37:23.074 --> 00:37:24.976
-He's here! -Who's here?

576
00:37:25.009 --> 00:37:28.045
Who-- Me! I'm here.

577
00:37:28.079 --> 00:37:30.081
[laughs] You're funny, Dad.

578
00:37:30.114 --> 00:37:32.850
I'm a laugh a minute. Where's my off button?

579
00:37:32.883 --> 00:37:34.852
Come on. Let's get you back to Mom.

580
00:37:39.523 --> 00:37:40.891
[Elizabeth] Chase?

581
00:37:42.893 --> 00:37:44.729
Check this out, Mom!

582
00:37:47.632 --> 00:37:50.768
[cheers and applause]

583
00:37:52.136 --> 00:37:53.771
Thank you. Thank you. Yeah.

584
00:37:54.005 --> 00:37:55.773
Oh, no autographs, please.

585
00:37:56.841 --> 00:38:00.478
That's beautiful, but let's go. We're supposed to stay together.

586
00:38:15.893 --> 00:38:18.796
[singing]

587
00:38:27.038 --> 00:38:29.573
[Stretch] Come one, come all. Before your very eyes,

588
00:38:29.607 --> 00:38:32.677
Harbin's largest collection of rarities!

589
00:38:32.710 --> 00:38:36.380
You, my friend. You! Yes, you.

590
00:38:36.414 --> 00:38:39.917
I got pandas and snow tigers and monkeys of every kind,

591
00:38:40.418 --> 00:38:42.820
all belonging to Harbin's noble history.

592
00:38:43.954 --> 00:38:47.591
This is the real deal, kid. The deal that's real.

593
00:38:47.625 --> 00:38:49.694
One hundred percent seal.

594
00:38:52.930 --> 00:38:54.832
Ooh. What's that?

595
00:38:56.067 --> 00:38:58.402
Uh, shell-oculars.

596
00:38:58.436 --> 00:39:02.606
Made from genuine 100 percent pure plastic.

597
00:39:07.712 --> 00:39:10.147
[laughing]

598
00:39:13.584 --> 00:39:14.652
Oh, man.

599
00:39:14.852 --> 00:39:16.887
Let me guess. Pete?

600
00:39:17.088 --> 00:39:20.825
-No, I'm Repete. -And I'm Pete.

601
00:39:24.128 --> 00:39:26.030
[laughs] No, we're kidding.

602
00:39:26.063 --> 00:39:27.965
-I'm Pete. -And I'm Repete.

603
00:39:27.998 --> 00:39:30.034
[laughing]

604
00:39:30.067 --> 00:39:31.936
Oh, man. Every time.

605
00:39:31.969 --> 00:39:34.538
Oh, you've gotta love those twins.

606
00:39:34.572 --> 00:39:35.506
[laughing]

607
00:39:40.511 --> 00:39:42.880
-I'll take it! -That'll be 20 cubes.

608
00:39:43.781 --> 00:39:46.117
I don't have any money on me right now.

609
00:39:46.150 --> 00:39:47.852
[sighs] Seriously?

610
00:39:47.885 --> 00:39:51.756
But my dad is King of the North, I mean, he's good for it.

611
00:39:51.789 --> 00:39:53.657
King of the North? Yeah.

612
00:39:53.691 --> 00:39:55.860
And I'm the Dragon of the East.

613
00:39:55.893 --> 00:39:57.528
-[roars] -Huh?

614
00:39:57.561 --> 00:40:01.732
I was born at night, but I wasn't born last night.

615
00:40:01.766 --> 00:40:03.100
Give me that.

616
00:40:05.136 --> 00:40:06.537
[laughing]

617
00:40:08.806 --> 00:40:10.007
There you are!

618
00:40:10.708 --> 00:40:14.612
Norm! Watch where you're going. You hurt them.

619
00:40:14.645 --> 00:40:16.480
Oh, dear. Are you two all right?

620
00:40:16.514 --> 00:40:17.615
[Fu] They're fine.

621
00:40:18.716 --> 00:40:21.051
What am I going to do with you two?

622
00:40:21.085 --> 00:40:22.019
[both] Dad!

623
00:40:22.953 --> 00:40:23.921
What are you doing out of your workshop?

624
00:40:23.954 --> 00:40:27.491
Making sure my Frostbite 3000 is operational.

625
00:40:29.527 --> 00:40:30.561
[beeps]

626
00:40:31.629 --> 00:40:33.597
[whistles]

627
00:40:36.967 --> 00:40:40.271
[crowd gasping]

628
00:40:40.304 --> 00:40:42.940
[fireworks exploding]

629
00:40:46.677 --> 00:40:49.914
Master Fu, you are amazing!

630
00:40:50.648 --> 00:40:52.550
Good to see you, sir.

631
00:40:52.883 --> 00:40:54.919
Good to see you all.

632
00:40:54.952 --> 00:40:56.921
Sorry I haven't been out more.

633
00:40:57.121 --> 00:40:59.223
I've been... busy.

634
00:40:59.256 --> 00:41:01.091
It's okay, Mister Fu, sir.

635
00:41:01.125 --> 00:41:03.527
You honor us with your presence.

636
00:41:04.762 --> 00:41:05.863
Welcome to Harbin.

637
00:41:07.064 --> 00:41:11.535
I am Fu, Harbin designer, inventor, architect and father.

638
00:41:14.238 --> 00:41:17.274
You're him? I mean, he's you?

639
00:41:17.308 --> 00:41:20.277
You're the one who designed this entire city?

640
00:41:20.811 --> 00:41:24.815
[both] Every single thing you see.

641
00:41:24.849 --> 00:41:27.718
Oh, that's mega cool!

642
00:41:27.751 --> 00:41:29.186
I gotta say, I love your work.

643
00:41:29.220 --> 00:41:30.721
[Maria] Can I have your autograph?

644
00:41:30.754 --> 00:41:31.689
[Norm] Kids, come on.

645
00:41:31.722 --> 00:41:34.592
He's a designer, but your old man is a king.

646
00:41:34.892 --> 00:41:36.293
I thought so.

647
00:41:36.327 --> 00:41:38.696
You're Norm, the King of the North!

648
00:41:38.729 --> 00:41:41.131
-Guilty as charged. -Told ya.

649
00:41:41.165 --> 00:41:42.867
What brings you to Harbin?

650
00:41:42.900 --> 00:41:45.536
A long overdue family vacation.

651
00:41:45.769 --> 00:41:48.005
Just before the Northern Jubilee?

652
00:41:48.038 --> 00:41:49.039
Strange.

653
00:41:50.074 --> 00:41:52.810
It's never the wrong time for family fun, huh?

654
00:41:52.843 --> 00:41:54.778
Are you staying for the weekend?

655
00:41:54.812 --> 00:41:57.047
My birthday is coming up, and I would be honored

656
00:41:57.081 --> 00:41:58.148
to have you join me.

657
00:41:58.182 --> 00:41:59.183
What? No!

658
00:42:00.284 --> 00:42:02.319
Dad, we thought it was just gonna be the three of us

659
00:42:02.353 --> 00:42:04.822
-for your birthday this year. -Thanks for the offer,

660
00:42:04.855 --> 00:42:06.624
but we won't be staying that long.

661
00:42:06.657 --> 00:42:08.759
We all have to get back to the North for the Jubilee.

662
00:42:09.126 --> 00:42:11.061
-[both] Phew! -[Fu] I understand.

663
00:42:11.262 --> 00:42:13.931
Well then, it would be my honor

664
00:42:13.964 --> 00:42:17.167
to at least invite all of you for dinner tonight.

665
00:42:17.201 --> 00:42:18.936
-We can't. -We'd love to.

666
00:42:19.136 --> 00:42:21.205
-Oh. -I can't.

667
00:42:22.273 --> 00:42:23.707
It'll be our pleasure.

668
00:42:26.143 --> 00:42:27.778
We'll be there.

669
00:42:29.013 --> 00:42:29.980
Excellent.

670
00:42:31.115 --> 00:42:33.784
Now, if you'll excuse me, I must return to my work.

671
00:42:38.789 --> 00:42:41.158
[grunts] What do you mean, you can't?

672
00:42:41.191 --> 00:42:42.860
We're on a family vacation.

673
00:42:42.893 --> 00:42:43.928
I know.

674
00:42:45.029 --> 00:42:46.864
Uh, look, I have plans. Things to do, people to see.

675
00:42:46.897 --> 00:42:47.998
I'll explain later.

676
00:42:54.238 --> 00:42:55.272
[sighs]

677
00:42:58.208 --> 00:42:59.677
[squeaking]

678
00:43:00.044 --> 00:43:01.912
[whirring]

679
00:43:04.181 --> 00:43:06.917
[screaming]

680
00:43:15.292 --> 00:43:17.127
[screaming]

681
00:43:24.234 --> 00:43:26.337
Look! It's snowing!

682
00:44:12.850 --> 00:44:14.785
[sniffing] Ha!

683
00:44:17.821 --> 00:44:18.822
[groans]

684
00:44:20.090 --> 00:44:21.425
-[goat bleats] -What?

685
00:44:22.493 --> 00:44:24.328
Hmm. Hmm?

686
00:44:25.195 --> 00:44:27.031
[bleats]

687
00:44:39.810 --> 00:44:40.844
Hmm.

688
00:44:43.280 --> 00:44:45.482
Thank you, Fu. Dinner was delicious.

689
00:44:45.983 --> 00:44:47.484
[chuckles] You're too kind.

690
00:44:49.553 --> 00:44:50.988
Wow!

691
00:44:51.255 --> 00:44:52.456
[Chase gasps]

692
00:44:52.489 --> 00:44:54.124
Cool!

693
00:44:54.158 --> 00:44:55.926
[Maria] So pretty!

694
00:44:56.126 --> 00:44:58.128
Look at all those trophies.

695
00:44:58.929 --> 00:45:01.265
-You must be so proud. -Oh, yeah.

696
00:45:01.298 --> 00:45:04.101
Skiing was my favorite thing to do with my family.

697
00:45:04.401 --> 00:45:06.203
Why did you stop?

698
00:45:06.236 --> 00:45:08.372
Well, Harbin takes up all of my time.

699
00:45:08.405 --> 00:45:11.308
Cities don't build themselves, you know.

700
00:45:11.341 --> 00:45:12.409
Who knows?

701
00:45:13.510 --> 00:45:15.245
Maybe if our father was made a king like your father,

702
00:45:15.279 --> 00:45:16.914
he'd have the time to take ski vacations

703
00:45:16.947 --> 00:45:20.050
-with his family again. -And watch me win?

704
00:45:20.084 --> 00:45:23.153
Uh, yeah, right. He never beats me.

705
00:45:23.187 --> 00:45:26.123
[laughs] So, by never, you mean all the time?

706
00:45:26.156 --> 00:45:28.092
-I own him. -In your dreams!

707
00:45:28.125 --> 00:45:30.027
Boys, please.

708
00:45:30.561 --> 00:45:32.529
-Sorry. -Yeah. Sorry.

709
00:45:32.563 --> 00:45:35.232
-I'm more sorry! -Nuh-uh! I'm more sorry!

710
00:45:38.235 --> 00:45:40.270
[both] You guys are really lucky.

711
00:45:41.038 --> 00:45:42.072
[laughs]

712
00:45:42.106 --> 00:45:43.507
-You have no idea. -As if!

713
00:45:44.541 --> 00:45:45.976
Oh, you're serious?

714
00:45:46.543 --> 00:45:47.945
[Fu] Come, now.

715
00:45:47.978 --> 00:45:50.414
I've had the guest room prepared for you.

716
00:45:52.416 --> 00:45:55.786
-[rumbling] -[laughing]

717
00:45:56.120 --> 00:45:57.387
What was that?

718
00:45:57.621 --> 00:46:00.390
Why, that's just the Slide to the Heavens.

719
00:46:00.424 --> 00:46:02.893
It goes right through the main hall.

720
00:46:18.142 --> 00:46:20.010
[sniffs] Ha!

721
00:46:37.961 --> 00:46:39.096
[groans]

722
00:46:39.129 --> 00:46:42.132
Oh, man. I hate stairs.

723
00:46:42.166 --> 00:46:43.233
[sighs]

724
00:46:43.600 --> 00:46:45.903
[laughing]

725
00:46:50.007 --> 00:46:51.074
Easy.

726
00:46:53.277 --> 00:46:55.279
[humming]

727
00:47:02.252 --> 00:47:04.221
[groans]

728
00:47:11.695 --> 00:47:16.033
[panting]

729
00:47:19.436 --> 00:47:20.971
[gasps]

730
00:47:21.004 --> 00:47:22.272
Fu stole my crown!

731
00:47:22.639 --> 00:47:24.041
[screams]

732
00:47:24.074 --> 00:47:27.077
[groaning]

733
00:47:33.984 --> 00:47:35.052
Huh?

734
00:48:15.325 --> 00:48:16.326
Ha!

735
00:48:18.095 --> 00:48:20.364
[grunting]

736
00:48:25.669 --> 00:48:27.170
[groans]

737
00:48:27.204 --> 00:48:30.040
[grunting]

738
00:48:36.280 --> 00:48:37.481
That's half.

739
00:48:37.514 --> 00:48:40.684
[grunting]

740
00:48:40.717 --> 00:48:42.686
That's just bad architecture.

741
00:48:44.187 --> 00:48:45.389
Gotcha!

742
00:48:48.025 --> 00:48:49.593
Oh, man!

743
00:48:49.793 --> 00:48:52.663
[door closing]

744
00:48:52.696 --> 00:48:53.697
Oh, no.

745
00:49:05.375 --> 00:49:06.610
[gasps]

746
00:49:09.746 --> 00:49:11.214
-[beeps] -[phone ringing]

747
00:49:11.248 --> 00:49:12.249
-[Norm] Yello? -Norm?

748
00:49:13.317 --> 00:49:14.151
[Norm] You've reached Norm's summer home.

749
00:49:14.184 --> 00:49:16.053
Some are home, some are not. [laughs]

750
00:49:16.353 --> 00:49:17.521
Leave a message at the beep.

751
00:49:17.554 --> 00:49:19.189
-[beeps] -[groans]

752
00:49:19.222 --> 00:49:22.726
Two days, Norm! We've only got two days left!

753
00:49:22.759 --> 00:49:25.462
If it gets out that you've lost your crown,

754
00:49:25.495 --> 00:49:27.764
everyone's gonna freak out!

755
00:49:27.798 --> 00:49:29.099
[beeps]

756
00:49:30.600 --> 00:49:32.235
[clears throat, gasps]

757
00:49:32.602 --> 00:49:35.539
[screaming]

758
00:49:43.780 --> 00:49:46.216
Quiet!

759
00:49:49.553 --> 00:49:51.722
Calm down!

760
00:49:53.390 --> 00:49:56.193
Yes, the crown has gone missing,

761
00:49:56.226 --> 00:49:59.563
but Norm is doing everything in his power to fix it.

762
00:49:59.596 --> 00:50:03.066
-So... keep calm... -[squeaks]

763
00:50:05.369 --> 00:50:07.270
...and Jubilee on.

764
00:50:08.672 --> 00:50:11.708
[screaming]

765
00:50:12.409 --> 00:50:14.678
Norm has lost the crown.

766
00:50:14.711 --> 00:50:17.714
The Jubilee is approaching and our very existence

767
00:50:17.748 --> 00:50:19.483
is now at risk.

768
00:50:19.516 --> 00:50:21.718
Yep. Things are definitely curdling

769
00:50:21.752 --> 00:50:25.155
in the old butter mill of disaster there, Jim.

770
00:50:36.833 --> 00:50:38.502
[yawns]

771
00:50:39.369 --> 00:50:41.138
Huh? Norm?

772
00:50:45.442 --> 00:50:46.843
[groans] Get out of here.

773
00:50:51.581 --> 00:50:53.817
Uh, where's your father?

774
00:50:54.684 --> 00:50:56.420
-No idea. -No clue.

775
00:50:56.453 --> 00:50:58.321
Guys, I think your dad is in trouble.

776
00:50:58.355 --> 00:50:59.790
Dad? In trouble?

777
00:50:59.823 --> 00:51:02.325
-Shocker. -He's probably still working.

778
00:51:02.359 --> 00:51:05.862
Yeah. "The crown never rests." [imitates chicken]

779
00:51:05.896 --> 00:51:08.698
[Elizabeth] No, Dad always comes home.

780
00:51:08.732 --> 00:51:11.468
If he's not here, it means trouble.

781
00:51:11.835 --> 00:51:14.237
Mission improbable. Find Dad.

782
00:51:14.271 --> 00:51:17.207
-Booyah! -Quinn, you take the fair.

783
00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:19.176
Maria, you take the ski slope.

784
00:51:19.209 --> 00:51:20.510
-Chase-- -I'm on the rides!

785
00:51:20.911 --> 00:51:23.613
Operation Dad Retrieval is a go!

786
00:51:27.651 --> 00:51:30.420
First rule of Dad, he is always probably

787
00:51:30.454 --> 00:51:32.355
where you least expect him to be.

788
00:51:32.389 --> 00:51:35.525
Dad would never ski!

789
00:51:35.926 --> 00:51:38.361
Dad would never ride a roller coaster.

790
00:51:39.763 --> 00:51:42.265
Where's the last place Dad should be?

791
00:51:42.599 --> 00:51:44.634
That's probably where he is.

792
00:51:48.371 --> 00:51:49.773
I got nothing.

793
00:51:49.806 --> 00:51:51.708
[indistinct chatter]

794
00:51:57.914 --> 00:52:00.250
Where could he possibly be?

795
00:52:02.819 --> 00:52:04.387
[grunting]

796
00:52:10.861 --> 00:52:13.430
[grunts]

797
00:52:15.732 --> 00:52:17.367
[groans]

798
00:52:19.536 --> 00:52:20.770
[sighs]

799
00:52:29.412 --> 00:52:30.614
[sighs]

800
00:52:58.742 --> 00:53:00.477
[whistles, laughs]

801
00:53:04.414 --> 00:53:06.249
Huh? Hmm.

802
00:53:11.922 --> 00:53:13.256
-[phone vibrates] -[gasps]

803
00:53:14.457 --> 00:53:16.593
Hey, Pete. Talk to me, bro.

804
00:53:22.732 --> 00:53:24.467
[squeaking]

805
00:53:34.444 --> 00:53:35.445
[knocks]

806
00:53:36.379 --> 00:53:37.480
-[Norm] Hello? Who is this? -Shh.

807
00:53:37.514 --> 00:53:38.515
[Norm] Let me out!

808
00:53:39.816 --> 00:53:40.984
[squeaking]

809
00:53:41.017 --> 00:53:41.918
[farts]

810
00:53:42.953 --> 00:53:45.722
Lemmings! Thank heaven! It's a trap door.

811
00:53:45.755 --> 00:53:47.824
The trigger is one of the trophies,

812
00:53:48.525 --> 00:53:50.660
which I'm pretty sure half of them are fake.

813
00:53:50.694 --> 00:53:52.662
I mean, come on. No one's that good at anything.

814
00:54:00.937 --> 00:54:03.573
[Maria] Have you seen a big huggable polar bear

815
00:54:03.607 --> 00:54:07.344
about yay big and answers to the name of "Dad?"

816
00:54:07.377 --> 00:54:10.547
Only some of the time. Mostly, he's just "King."

817
00:54:10.747 --> 00:54:12.515
Uh, I don't know.

818
00:54:12.549 --> 00:54:16.720
He's not even in the nap caves. He loves naps and caves.

819
00:54:16.753 --> 00:54:18.822
Now I'm really concerned.

820
00:54:18.855 --> 00:54:20.290
Where's Chase?

821
00:54:27.364 --> 00:54:28.598
[burps]

822
00:54:28.632 --> 00:54:30.667
What? Nervous eating.

823
00:54:32.969 --> 00:54:35.505
Wait a minute. Maybe Fu can help.

824
00:54:54.124 --> 00:54:57.894
[panting]

825
00:55:02.666 --> 00:55:03.767
[grunting]

826
00:55:22.952 --> 00:55:24.587
[whirring]

827
00:55:31.828 --> 00:55:32.729
[gasps]

828
00:55:36.099 --> 00:55:38.802
What in the Northern Lights are you doing?

829
00:55:38.835 --> 00:55:41.871
Get down from there. Have you gone mad?

830
00:55:41.905 --> 00:55:43.973
You can't just destroy Fu's home.

831
00:55:44.574 --> 00:55:46.009
We're his guests here!

832
00:55:46.042 --> 00:55:48.845
-[Norm] Elizabeth! Is that you? -Norm?

833
00:55:49.446 --> 00:55:51.781
-Dad? -Norm, where are you?

834
00:55:51.815 --> 00:55:52.916
[Norm] Behind the trap door!

835
00:55:55.585 --> 00:55:57.153
[Elizabeth] What are you doing in there?

836
00:55:57.187 --> 00:55:59.489
[Norm] Well, I'm trapped.

837
00:55:59.689 --> 00:56:01.024
Of course!

838
00:56:01.057 --> 00:56:02.625
Getting trapped in a secret room

839
00:56:02.659 --> 00:56:04.894
is the last place you'd expect Dad to be.

840
00:56:13.536 --> 00:56:16.873
Was it not obvious to everyone that it was a trap statue?

841
00:56:21.845 --> 00:56:24.547
[grunts] Oh, hang on.

842
00:56:25.048 --> 00:56:27.617
Almost. I'm just gonna suck it in.

843
00:56:27.650 --> 00:56:28.852
[sighs]

844
00:56:32.122 --> 00:56:33.957
[laughs]

845
00:56:36.626 --> 00:56:39.729
[grunting]

846
00:56:42.532 --> 00:56:44.734
Oh, I missed you all so much!

847
00:56:44.768 --> 00:56:47.203
Oh, I thought I'd never see you guys again.

848
00:56:47.237 --> 00:56:49.139
I'm so happy. I'm so relieved.

849
00:56:49.172 --> 00:56:50.940
-I'm so-- -Not telling us

850
00:56:50.974 --> 00:56:52.175
what's really going on.

851
00:56:52.976 --> 00:56:54.978
Uh, what are you implying?

852
00:56:55.578 --> 00:56:56.880
Enough of that, Norm.

853
00:56:56.913 --> 00:56:58.748
You've been acting weird since day one.

854
00:56:58.782 --> 00:57:00.016
What are you hiding?

855
00:57:00.049 --> 00:57:02.786
You won't think the same of me if I tell you.

856
00:57:03.653 --> 00:57:05.822
There's nothing you can't tell us.

857
00:57:06.022 --> 00:57:07.891
-Right, kids? -[kids] Right!

858
00:57:08.958 --> 00:57:12.095
Well, the truth is...

859
00:57:12.128 --> 00:57:13.530
[Elizabeth] You did what?

860
00:57:15.999 --> 00:57:19.169
-I should've known. Classic Dad. -What are you talking about?

861
00:57:19.202 --> 00:57:22.005
This trip was never about spending time with us.

862
00:57:22.038 --> 00:57:24.808
It was about you and that stupid crown.

863
00:57:24.841 --> 00:57:26.976
No! Well, yes.

864
00:57:27.010 --> 00:57:30.780
Well, it wasn't at first, but it is now.

865
00:57:30.814 --> 00:57:33.016
You know that you're all that matters to me.

866
00:57:33.049 --> 00:57:35.218
-Are we? -Of course you are,

867
00:57:35.251 --> 00:57:36.853
but if I don't retrieve the crown

868
00:57:36.886 --> 00:57:39.589
before the beginning of winter at the Jubilee tomorrow,

869
00:57:39.622 --> 00:57:42.158
an endless winter will fall upon the North

870
00:57:42.192 --> 00:57:44.060
and I'll be known as the worst king ever.

871
00:57:44.093 --> 00:57:46.095
That's not the only thing you'll be known as.

872
00:57:46.129 --> 00:57:47.697
Quinn, stop.

873
00:57:47.730 --> 00:57:49.065
No, he's right.

874
00:57:49.098 --> 00:57:50.934
I haven't been the best dad recently.

875
00:57:50.967 --> 00:57:54.137
Recently? Try ever since you became king!

876
00:57:54.170 --> 00:57:55.071
Quinn!

877
00:57:55.772 --> 00:57:56.773
No, Quinn. Come on.

878
00:57:58.074 --> 00:57:59.709
[Maria] Come back!

879
00:58:00.643 --> 00:58:03.913
I heard yelling and-- Dear heavens, my awards!

880
00:58:05.782 --> 00:58:07.584
What have you done to my beautiful trophies?

881
00:58:07.784 --> 00:58:09.219
[scoffs] Your trophies?

882
00:58:09.252 --> 00:58:11.254
What have you done with my crown?

883
00:58:12.589 --> 00:58:14.991
And what in the world is that room?

884
00:58:15.325 --> 00:58:17.827
Oh, don't give me that.

885
00:58:17.861 --> 00:58:19.562
I'm on to you, Fu.

886
00:58:19.596 --> 00:58:21.130
All these fake awards mean nothing

887
00:58:21.164 --> 00:58:24.300
without the one true trophy, my crown.

888
00:58:24.334 --> 00:58:27.136
I don't have any idea what you're talking about.

889
00:58:27.170 --> 00:58:28.204
Oh, yeah?

890
00:58:28.238 --> 00:58:29.873
Then how do you explain...

891
00:58:31.174 --> 00:58:32.208
this?

892
00:58:32.242 --> 00:58:33.276
Dear heavens.

893
00:58:36.379 --> 00:58:39.749
-I've been robbed. -Oh, don't play dumb.

894
00:58:39.782 --> 00:58:41.985
I know you stole my crown, Fu.

895
00:58:42.018 --> 00:58:42.919
The skis...

896
00:58:44.020 --> 00:58:46.823
the mask, the gloves...

897
00:58:48.992 --> 00:58:52.228
the frost-pedo, everything points to you.

898
00:58:53.096 --> 00:58:56.199
On my honor, I didn't take your crown.

899
00:58:59.636 --> 00:59:02.872
-See? My key is gone! -Huh?

900
00:59:03.273 --> 00:59:06.943
The only people that know where I keep it are me and my...

901
00:59:11.414 --> 00:59:13.149
[both] The twins!

902
00:59:30.767 --> 00:59:32.101
There! Tracks!

903
00:59:43.046 --> 00:59:44.681
They're good kids.

904
00:59:44.714 --> 00:59:47.116
I don't know why they'd do such a thing.

905
00:59:48.851 --> 00:59:51.754
Excuse me. I'm so ashamed.

906
00:59:55.858 --> 00:59:57.727
[grunts] Fu, wait!

907
01:00:16.145 --> 01:00:17.981
[wind whistling]

908
01:00:32.428 --> 01:00:34.397
What in the world happened back there?

909
01:00:36.132 --> 01:00:37.166
[gasps]

910
01:00:37.200 --> 01:00:38.801
[sobbing]

911
01:00:38.835 --> 01:00:39.836
Fu?

912
01:00:40.336 --> 01:00:41.704
Oh, no.

913
01:00:42.138 --> 01:00:43.239
Don't cry.

914
01:00:43.506 --> 01:00:47.043
It's okay. We all have bad days. [sniffs]

915
01:00:48.411 --> 01:00:51.414
[sobs] And your crying is making me sad too.

916
01:00:51.814 --> 01:00:55.418
[both crying]

917
01:00:59.455 --> 01:01:01.758
I forgive you. It's all good.

918
01:01:03.059 --> 01:01:05.261
I mean, kids can do some crazy things.

919
01:01:05.495 --> 01:01:06.763
Take Chase.

920
01:01:06.796 --> 01:01:08.431
He once ate an entire wedding cake

921
01:01:08.464 --> 01:01:10.800
and he wasn't even invited to the wedding.

922
01:01:11.801 --> 01:01:13.102
It's not that.

923
01:01:13.136 --> 01:01:17.273
I just feel so much pressure to make my twins proud.

924
01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:21.177
That's really why I work so hard on Harbin.

925
01:01:23.346 --> 01:01:26.049
That they would be proud of their father.

926
01:01:26.349 --> 01:01:28.785
But you're such a big, strong tiger.

927
01:01:28.985 --> 01:01:31.354
They even built a statue just for you.

928
01:01:32.155 --> 01:01:34.924
That was just the twins trying to cheer me up.

929
01:01:37.160 --> 01:01:39.128
They deserve better than me.

930
01:01:41.330 --> 01:01:43.266
Being a dad is hard,

931
01:01:43.466 --> 01:01:46.235
especially when you have an entire city counting on you.

932
01:01:46.436 --> 01:01:47.970
So are my kids.

933
01:01:48.271 --> 01:01:51.174
Trust me, your kids love you...

934
01:01:52.008 --> 01:01:53.476
even if they don't know the real trouble

935
01:01:53.509 --> 01:01:54.944
they're causing.

936
01:01:57.513 --> 01:01:59.415
I need your help, Fu.

937
01:01:59.449 --> 01:02:01.918
The North is counting on me to return with the crown,

938
01:02:01.951 --> 01:02:03.086
like, yesterday.

939
01:02:03.119 --> 01:02:04.887
Do you know where they might have it?

940
01:02:10.426 --> 01:02:11.527
Follow me.

941
01:02:15.965 --> 01:02:18.101
-We got your text. -Thanks for coming.

942
01:02:18.134 --> 01:02:20.536
Always, Dad. We're a family.

943
01:02:27.910 --> 01:02:29.178
Yeah, we are.

944
01:02:30.947 --> 01:02:32.081
Hmm.

945
01:02:32.115 --> 01:02:33.983
There's only one place where my twins

946
01:02:34.016 --> 01:02:35.418
could be hiding your crown.

947
01:02:36.018 --> 01:02:38.221
Nothing is gonna stop us now!

948
01:02:39.922 --> 01:02:42.825
Nothing except maybe that icy ascent.

949
01:02:42.859 --> 01:02:45.061
[lemmings yodel]

950
01:03:02.578 --> 01:03:05.248
I guess it could be worse. It could be snowing.

951
01:03:05.281 --> 01:03:08.484
[thunder rumbles]

952
01:03:11.154 --> 01:03:14.991
[groans] It's worse than worse. I can't do this.

953
01:03:15.258 --> 01:03:18.828
You can do this, Dad. You're King of the North.

954
01:03:19.095 --> 01:03:21.297
Even more than that, you're my dad.

955
01:03:21.330 --> 01:03:22.932
[both] Our dad!

956
01:03:23.132 --> 01:03:24.901
[Elizabeth] The king of our family.

957
01:03:32.108 --> 01:03:33.576
I can do this!

958
01:03:40.483 --> 01:03:41.984
[button buzzing]

959
01:03:46.389 --> 01:03:48.357
[groans] You're kidding me, right?

960
01:03:48.391 --> 01:03:51.127
What? It was such a nice family moment.

961
01:03:51.394 --> 01:03:54.463
I mean, you could climb the side of this peak

962
01:03:54.497 --> 01:03:57.166
or we could just go inside.

963
01:03:59.435 --> 01:04:00.436
Good idea.

964
01:04:05.174 --> 01:04:07.043
What is this place?

965
01:04:07.076 --> 01:04:09.178
This was our old family home.

966
01:04:09.445 --> 01:04:11.480
I built this place a long time ago

967
01:04:11.514 --> 01:04:13.382
to protect my family from danger.

968
01:04:14.150 --> 01:04:15.484
-It's booby-trapped. -Huh?

969
01:04:15.518 --> 01:04:18.287
Only the twins and I know where all the traps are.

970
01:04:22.358 --> 01:04:23.626
Okay, then.

971
01:04:24.360 --> 01:04:25.361
After you.

972
01:04:27.663 --> 01:04:30.566
Just follow my every step and we'll be completely...

973
01:04:32.201 --> 01:04:33.402
[groans]

974
01:04:33.436 --> 01:04:36.339
...safe!

975
01:04:39.575 --> 01:04:41.677
Okay, so the first step's a doozy.

976
01:04:45.481 --> 01:04:47.316
I better do this alone.

977
01:04:47.350 --> 01:04:50.152
No way, Dad. We want in on the fun.

978
01:04:51.053 --> 01:04:54.090
-You guys are with me? -This is a family affair.

979
01:04:54.123 --> 01:04:55.324
After you, Dad.

980
01:05:09.038 --> 01:05:10.239
Hmm?

981
01:05:15.311 --> 01:05:16.979
Heavens to polar bear.

982
01:05:17.013 --> 01:05:18.581
We're not gonna be ready in time!

983
01:05:19.181 --> 01:05:20.349
[squeaking]

984
01:05:37.433 --> 01:05:38.501
[screaming]

985
01:05:47.576 --> 01:05:50.713
[cheering]

986
01:05:55.551 --> 01:05:58.354
Everything is in place for a great Jubilee

987
01:05:58.387 --> 01:06:01.324
except for Norm and the crown.

988
01:06:01.357 --> 01:06:03.025
I'll tell ya, Rick,

989
01:06:03.059 --> 01:06:06.228
it's all about how badly Norm wants it.

990
01:06:06.262 --> 01:06:07.697
Does he have what it takes?

991
01:06:07.730 --> 01:06:10.633
He'll have to give 110 percent.

992
01:06:10.666 --> 01:06:13.369
Maybe even 111, Jim.

993
01:06:13.402 --> 01:06:15.771
It's gut check time, Rick.

994
01:06:15.805 --> 01:06:17.707
And you know that that Norm there,

995
01:06:17.740 --> 01:06:19.775
he's got a real gut.

996
01:06:22.345 --> 01:06:24.747
[stomach rumbling]

997
01:06:39.562 --> 01:06:41.163
[panting]

998
01:06:53.175 --> 01:06:54.176
Any ideas?

999
01:06:54.610 --> 01:06:56.145
-Over there. -This way!

1000
01:06:56.178 --> 01:06:57.346
That way!

1001
01:07:03.486 --> 01:07:05.521
I've got something. This way!

1002
01:07:06.255 --> 01:07:07.189
Are you sure?

1003
01:07:07.490 --> 01:07:08.724
One way to find out.

1004
01:07:08.758 --> 01:07:09.658
[beeping]

1005
01:07:11.527 --> 01:07:14.697
Pete, Repete, this is your father, Fu.

1006
01:07:17.166 --> 01:07:20.469
[Fu's voice] Pete, Repete, this is your father, Fu.

1007
01:07:20.503 --> 01:07:21.771
This is your father, Fu.

1008
01:07:22.671 --> 01:07:24.573
Nice try, Quinn, but they're never gonna fall

1009
01:07:24.607 --> 01:07:27.176
-for something like-- -[Repete] Dad? Is that you?

1010
01:07:28.744 --> 01:07:30.146
You were saying?

1011
01:07:32.615 --> 01:07:33.682
[floor clicks]

1012
01:07:33.716 --> 01:07:34.817
Huh?

1013
01:07:37.853 --> 01:07:39.155
Oh, no!

1014
01:07:59.575 --> 01:08:00.543
[screaming]

1015
01:08:09.785 --> 01:08:10.753
[screaming]

1016
01:08:16.625 --> 01:08:19.728
[grunting]

1017
01:08:20.863 --> 01:08:21.764
[groans]

1018
01:08:25.868 --> 01:08:28.838
Snow Blast!

1019
01:08:40.616 --> 01:08:41.517
Yes!

1020
01:08:46.555 --> 01:08:47.656
[laughs]

1021
01:08:54.964 --> 01:08:56.465
[squeaking]

1022
01:09:07.343 --> 01:09:08.277
Ha!

1023
01:09:16.418 --> 01:09:17.353
[chuckles]

1024
01:09:34.670 --> 01:09:36.338
Yeah, woo! Yeah!

1025
01:09:43.846 --> 01:09:44.880
[laughing]

1026
01:09:51.453 --> 01:09:53.756
[grunting]

1027
01:10:04.934 --> 01:10:07.403
[laughing]

1028
01:10:10.306 --> 01:10:13.375
-[music playing] -[indistinct chatter]

1029
01:10:25.654 --> 01:10:28.657
[indistinct chatter]

1030
01:10:33.429 --> 01:10:34.663
[record scratching]

1031
01:10:42.838 --> 01:10:45.374
[grunting]

1032
01:10:50.579 --> 01:10:51.513
[door opens]

1033
01:10:53.415 --> 01:10:54.917
[Repete] Dad, over here!

1034
01:10:54.950 --> 01:10:57.519
[machine powering up]

1035
01:11:03.592 --> 01:11:07.930
-Dad, are you okay? -[echoing]

1036
01:11:08.764 --> 01:11:10.566
Maybe we should go out and find him?

1037
01:11:11.533 --> 01:11:12.701
I'll go first.

1038
01:11:14.436 --> 01:11:15.537
No way!

1039
01:11:16.405 --> 01:11:17.806
I'll go first.

1040
01:11:17.840 --> 01:11:19.642
[laughs] No, I will.

1041
01:11:20.442 --> 01:11:22.077
As if! I got this.

1042
01:11:23.512 --> 01:11:24.580
[footsteps]

1043
01:11:27.783 --> 01:11:28.917
Dad?

1044
01:11:36.992 --> 01:11:38.360
Who's there?

1045
01:11:39.528 --> 01:11:41.930
Come out of hiding, whoever you really are.

1046
01:11:41.964 --> 01:11:44.933
It's me, Norm, King of the North.

1047
01:11:46.969 --> 01:11:48.337
-[camera clicks] -[groaning]

1048
01:11:48.637 --> 01:11:49.538
[Norm] Aha!

1049
01:11:50.139 --> 01:11:51.974
Come to papa bear.

1050
01:11:52.441 --> 01:11:54.910
Oh, yeah. That feels good.

1051
01:11:55.844 --> 01:11:57.613
Uh, you--

1052
01:11:57.646 --> 01:11:59.581
-I'm sorry. -I'm more sorry.

1053
01:12:02.117 --> 01:12:03.585
[both] We're both sorry.

1054
01:12:04.853 --> 01:12:07.122
We didn't mean to cause so many problems.

1055
01:12:07.156 --> 01:12:09.124
We just thought if we could give our father

1056
01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:11.493
a surprise crown for his birthday

1057
01:12:11.527 --> 01:12:13.495
and let him know how much we love him,

1058
01:12:13.529 --> 01:12:16.432
he might feel a little more, I don't know...

1059
01:12:16.699 --> 01:12:17.700
Kingly.

1060
01:12:36.485 --> 01:12:39.021
It's okay. I'm not mad at you.

1061
01:12:39.054 --> 01:12:40.756
You just wanted to help your father

1062
01:12:40.789 --> 01:12:42.624
feel better about himself.

1063
01:12:42.991 --> 01:12:46.495
But trust me, a crown does not make a king.

1064
01:12:47.830 --> 01:12:49.398
[Fu] Family does.

1065
01:12:50.165 --> 01:12:52.034
That's all that truly matters.

1066
01:12:58.907 --> 01:13:01.744
I'm so sorry I've been such a workaholic.

1067
01:13:02.044 --> 01:13:04.780
I love you guys so much.

1068
01:13:04.813 --> 01:13:07.015
-We love you too, Dad. -We love you too, Dad.

1069
01:13:21.530 --> 01:13:25.033
Just tell me how I can repay you, Norm, and I will.

1070
01:13:25.601 --> 01:13:26.568
Aw!

1071
01:13:27.102 --> 01:13:29.638
Aw, heck, I just love everybody.

1072
01:13:29.671 --> 01:13:32.107
Come on! Come here. Come here, you guys.

1073
01:13:32.141 --> 01:13:33.575
-Get over here! -[laughing]

1074
01:13:36.512 --> 01:13:38.013
-[cheering] -[whistling]

1075
01:13:38.280 --> 01:13:40.249
All right. Everyone in.

1076
01:13:40.282 --> 01:13:41.884
-[beeps] -It's picture time.

1077
01:13:45.788 --> 01:13:48.557
-[phone ringing] -[groans]

1078
01:13:48.891 --> 01:13:49.892
[phone beeps]

1079
01:13:50.559 --> 01:13:52.861
Whatever it is, it can wait.

1080
01:13:52.895 --> 01:13:55.998
[Socrates] This is an emergency, Norm!

1081
01:13:56.031 --> 01:13:57.933
This can't wait!

1082
01:13:57.966 --> 01:14:00.536
-The Jubilee's already begun! -[gasping]

1083
01:14:02.070 --> 01:14:03.138
[camera clicks]

1084
01:14:04.540 --> 01:14:07.943
-[music playing] -[indistinct chatter]

1085
01:14:11.847 --> 01:14:14.917
And the Jubilee festival has begun.

1086
01:14:14.950 --> 01:14:17.486
The pomp, the circumstance.

1087
01:14:17.686 --> 01:14:20.589
And I am pumped for the pomp.

1088
01:14:20.622 --> 01:14:24.092
Still no sign of Norm or the crown, Rick.

1089
01:14:25.194 --> 01:14:28.664
